### 1. Test Saga by creating a full Order (Using the main OrderController)
# This will save the order in DB and trigger the saga
POST http://localhost:8085/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000",
  "shippingAddress": "123 Test Street, Test City",
  "billingAddress": "123 Test Street, Test City",
  "currency": "INR",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174001",
      "productName": "Saga Test Product",
      "sku": "SKU-12345",
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitPrice": 500.00
    }
  ]
}

### 2. Test Saga by publishing directly to Kafka (Using OrderTestKafkaController)
# Use this if you just want to simulate the order created event directly in Kafka
POST http://localhost:8085/api/orders/test/publish
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174002",
  "productId": "123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174001",
  "quantity": 2
}

### 3. Check Order Status (Verify if Saga updated the order)
GET http://localhost:8085/api/orders/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174002
Accept: application/json
